/* This template is intended to be used via https://openwrt.org/meta/create_new_device_page . */

Asus / TP-LINK OnHub TGR1900 is a 3x3 802.11ac AP with a quad-core Qualcomm IPQ8064 SoC, 1 GiB RAM, and 4 GiB eMMC storage. Its stock firmware is based on ChromeOS, including a bootloader based on [[https://coreboot.org/|Coreboot]] and [[https://libreboot.org/docs/depthcharge/|Depthcharge]], and can be convinced to run non-Google-signed software (such as OpenWrt) by entering Developer Mode.

ASUS OnHub SRT-AC1900 is a nearly-identical AP, with almost identical hardware specifications, and nearly identical stock firmware. Thus, much of this page applies to it as well.

The TP-Link uses a standard 12V barrel jack. The ASUS has a weird connector for 19V. Keep this in mind if you're buying on eBay, since many listings won't include the power supply.
